  "final_output": "## Root cause\nCatalog v1.9.0 rolled out at 11:12 UTC and changed the default list sort to supplier_rank. For large categories, the read replica does a sequential scan and top-N sort before returning the list.\n\n## Evidence\nCatalog endpoint samples show slow GET /products. Trace 0410e5e2d3e8b68bb20ee077fe0c1c24 spends most of its time in the replica SELECT and shows the sort plan. Replica lag stayed near baseline. Catalog p95 stayed between about 315 and 432 ms through noon. The slow list reads drove up gateway p95 from 11:12. The gateway latency warning fired at 11:22 after 10 minutes and was still firing at noon.\n\n## Customer impact\nLarge product lists still return HTTP 200 but load much more slowly. Product detail p95 stayed low. The 11:37 GC pause came after the sustained p95 increase. Checkout success averaged close to the immediately preceding window. The available evidence supports a browsing slowdown, and it gives no reason to attribute isolated payment dips to this sort change.\n\n## Next steps\nRoll back Catalog to v1.8.2 or revert the default sort now. Check that product list p95 and replica query latency return to normal. Test the query plan on large categories before enabling the sort again."
}
